01:11:34,736 --> 01:11:40,736
Walk the Line is a 2005 American biographical
drama film directed by James Mangold.

11
01:18:44,210 --> 01:18:50,210
The screenplay, written by Mangold and Gill Dennis, is based on two autobiographies by the American singer-songwriter
Johnny Cash:  Man in Black: His Own Story in His Own Words (1975) and Cash: The Autobiography (1997).

12
01:25:53,684 --> 01:25:59,684
The film follows Cash's early life, his romance with the singer June Carter,
his ascent in the country music scene, and his drug addiction.

13
01:33:03,157 --> 01:33:09,157
It stars Joaquin Phoenix as Cash, Reese Witherspoon as Carter, Ginnifer Goodwin as
Cash's first wife Vivian Liberto, and Robert Patrick as Cash's father.

14
01:40:12,631 --> 01:40:18,631
Walk the Line premiered at the Telluride Film Festival on September 4, 2005, and
was theatrically released by  20th Century Fox on November 18.

15
01:47:22,105 --> 01:47:28,105
It received positive reviews and was a  box office success,
grossing $187 million on a $28 million budget.

16
01:54:31,578 --> 01:54:37,578
At the 78th Academy Awards, Witherspoon won Best Actress while the film was also nominated for
Best Actor (Phoenix), Best Sound Mixing, Best Costume Design and Best Film Editing.

17
02:01:41,052 --> 02:01:47,052
The film explores themes of prison, adultery,
concert, music record, country music.

